Each file here is its source byte for byte except its import lines: the
kernel's paths become @hm/kernel/{calendar,money} (the same bytes;
packages/kernel/VENDORED_FROM). None of the three imports a sibling. Nothing
else may be edited: src/__tests__/lossmit.test.ts compares each pair with
their import lines removed, compares the import lines after that one
rewrite, and fails on any difference. Lint and Prettier skip this directory
for the reason they skip the vendored trees.

evaluation.ts is the F-2-10 hierarchy walk (§12.2) and Regulation X's tier
and decision windows; plans.ts is the forbearance term and its caps (§12.4)
and the repayment plan's term search (§12.5); deferral.ts is the payment
deferral's screen, its non-interest-bearing balance, its new payment and its
completion timeline (§12.6). Each is pure: no clock, no randomness, no I/O.

ops.ts is not ported: it imports the Flex Modification and liquidation
engines, the application module and the kernel's ledger and events. The few
of its lines v1 needs (the arrears, the cap structure's installments to pay,
the term computation, the Reg X short-term test of a forbearance, the late
charges a deferral waives) are restated in src/lossmit/grader.ts with the
lines they come from, and a test holds those lines to the service's source.

To take a change from the servicing app, copy the three files again and
rewrite the same eight imports.
